# 14. NETWORK CONNECTION SYSTEM

Implement session establishment as a separate subsystem.

Sequence:

1. Generate session identifier.
2. Generate short-lived pairing material.
3. Publish signaling information.
4. Exchange capabilities.
5. Authenticate peer.
6. Attempt direct connectivity.
7. Select a supported transport.
8. Request receiver acceptance.
9. Establish transfer session.
10. Start data movement.

The signaling server must not receive file contents or private session keys.

Use short-lived credentials.

Expire unused pairing sessions.

Prevent pairing replay.

Do not treat possession of a publicly exposed session identifier as sufficient authentication.

QR codes must not contain permanent secrets.

